{"at": "2026-11-19T05:39:06Z", "class": ["data"], "evidence": ["run:20261119-053222-935a429e.log"], "id": "b48d6c955c468d8a", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "d6585485-cf53-539f-939a-17eb9ce72399", "signal": "rework", "text": "A ratio of two cities' median wages over all filings is biased by the mix of occupations (a city whose filings are mostly software jobs looks far richer). Compare the same occupation and wage level and take a weighted median over the shared cells.", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-19T05:39:07Z", "class": ["operations"], "evidence": ["run:20261119-053222-935a429e.log"], "id": "5c17e6c2a4093af7", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "d6585485-cf53-539f-939a-17eb9ce72399", "signal": "rework", "text": "A page generator that is not in the documented rebuild chain goes stale without anyone noticing: a company page still listed roles the list's newer rules had removed. After a rule change, run every generator of derived pages and diff the result, and name each generator in the update guide.", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-19T05:39:07Z", "class": ["data"], "evidence": ["run:20261119-053222-935a429e.log"], "id": "1397a4a045b58515", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "d6585485-cf53-539f-939a-17eb9ce72399", "signal": "rework", "text": "In a merge of research results, a row whose identity was confirmed must replace an unconfirmed one whatever its other figures, and 'searched, nothing found' must replace a 'not searched' placeholder; otherwise the same items are handed out for research again.", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-19T05:39:07Z", "class": ["language"], "evidence": ["run:20261119-045652-935a429e.log"], "id": "de7b9c037e8036bd", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "d6585485-cf53-539f-939a-17eb9ce72399", "signal": "first-success", "text": "When the owner adds a fact about himself mid-session, store it once in the profile with his words and date, then roll it into every document by a script with per-file edits and the same checks, and fit it by swapping weaker lines rather than shrinking type: 16 one-page documents were updated and re-checked in two passes.", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-19T05:40:11Z", "class": ["career"], "evidence": ["run:20261119-053222-935a429e.log"], "id": "51ca59f014b72f61", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "d6585485-cf53-539f-939a-17eb9ce72399", "signal": "rework", "text": "Job search: a rule that finds no gap is not proof of a match. Claim 'meets every requirement' only when the posting's own text was read. For the top of a ranked list, have a model read each posting's required asks against a one-page record card and quote every gap, and check by script that each quote is in the text: 112 of 167 top postings had a gap the rules missed.", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-19T05:40:11Z", "class": ["career"], "evidence": ["run:20261119-053222-935a429e.log"], "id": "1d52082c4e88b17b", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "d6585485-cf53-539f-939a-17eb9ce72399", "signal": "first-success", "text": "Before accepting a list of unreadable careers pages, probe every unread host once for the markup of known career-site systems. One probe of 1,414 hosts for one such system found 33 employers a plain reader handles, among them the largest local employer.", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-19T05:40:11Z", "class": ["operations"], "evidence": ["run:20261119-053222-935a429e.log"], "id": "26c6d2a786b3edce", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "d6585485-cf53-539f-939a-17eb9ce72399", "signal": "gate-failed", "text": "Do not run other heavy commands while a release gate with browser journeys runs: one journey measured a button during its animation and failed under load, then passed alone. Start the release last, on a quiet machine, and keep only light work beside it.", "trust": "observed"}
